**📋 PR Summary**

This PR fixes FastCGI response streaming for content types other than `text/event-stream`. Previously `strconv.ParseInt("", ...)` failed silently and left `resp.ContentLength` at `0` when a response carried no `Content-Length` header, causing `httputil.ReverseProxy` to treat unknown-length streamed responses as complete and buffer them. The fix defaults `ContentLength` to `-1` (net/http's spelling of unknown length) and only parses the header when present, and adds a unit test covering both the unknown- and known-length cases.

